    "intro_html":  "Ropa vieja means old clothes, which is what shredded beef in a pepper and tomato sauce apparently looked like to whoever named it. It is Cuba\u0027s national dish, and the olives at the end are not a garnish, they are the salt and the sharpness that make the whole thing sing. This wrap lands at about \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e, in a tortilla with 18 grams of fiber for 5 grams of net carb. We already run Ropa Vieja Rice Bowls, so this one takes a different road on purpose: a tomato paste and chicken broth base brightened with white wine vinegar, a little carrot for sweetness, all folded into a tortilla.",
