    "cost_closing_html":  "Swapping flank for sirloin is where the savings live, and the rest is pantry and a couple of peppers. Catch the steak on sale and the cost tab number drops with it.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSirloin does the flank\u0027s job for less.\u003c/strong\u003e Traditional ropa vieja uses flank, which the store prices like a treat. The board\u0027s sirloin gets to the same shredded place for a lot less, so buy that.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eGreen bell peppers are the traditional pick and the cheap one.\u003c/strong\u003e That alignment is rare, so take it and skip the pricier colored peppers here.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eTomato paste and broth build the sauce from the pantry.\u003c/strong\u003e A small can of paste and a box of broth cost almost nothing per serving and both keep for a long time."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cook the rice per the package and set it aside.",
                    "Season the sirloin with the cumin, oregano, salt, and black pepper and sear it in the olive oil, then add the sliced onion, green bell peppers, and carrot.",
                    "Stir the tomato paste into the chicken broth until smooth, pour it over the beef, cover, and braise until the meat shreds with a fork.",
                    "Shred the beef right in the pot and stir it back through the peppers and sauce.",
                    "Stir in the sliced green olives and the white wine vinegar and let it sit a few minutes off direct heat so the flavors settle.",
                    "Fold the cooked rice into the filling, then warm the tortillas and portion and wrap as below."
                ],
